  {"id":122234,"slug":"lithobius-forficatus","sci":"Lithobius forficatus","common":"Brown Centipede","family":"Lithobiidae","obs":96,"regions":[],"months":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,9,10,12],"photos":[{"id":179402948,"ext":"jpg","by":"Alexis Tinker-Tsavalas","lic":"CC BY"},{"id":244656993,"ext":"jpg","by":"Alexis Tinker-Tsavalas","lic":"CC BY"},{"id":171002593,"ext":"jpg","by":"Gilles San Martin","lic":"CC BY-SA"},{"id":171002603,"ext":"jpg","by":"Gilles San Martin","lic":"CC BY-SA"},{"id":166927181,"ext":"jpg","by":"Eugenijus Kavaliauskas","lic":"CC BY-NC"}],"wiki":"Lithobius forficatus","summary":"Lithobius forficatus, most commonly known as the brown centipede or stone centipede, is a common European centipede of the family Lithobiidae, although its distribution is not exclusive to Europe. It is between 18 and 30 mm long and up to 4 mm broad and is a chestnut brown color."},
